Patch from MiniMyth2 project

Developed-by: Piotr Oniszczuk <piotr.oniszczuk@gmail.com>
Signed-off-by: Piotr Oniszczuk <piotr.oniszczuk@gmail.com>




clk: meson: s4: peripherals: allow setting the CEC 32k clocks rate

The ceca_32k_clkout and cecb_32k_clkout gates propagate rate requests to
their parent, but the ceca_32k_sel and cecb_32k_sel muxes below them do
not, so clk_set_rate() on the CEC 32k outputs fails with -EINVAL and the
dual divider can never be configured through them.

Add CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT to both muxes, as is already done for the
sel_pre muxes and the clkout gates, so that the 32768Hz rate requested
by the CEC controller reaches the dual divider.

---
 drivers/clk/meson/s4-peripherals.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/meson/s4-peripherals.c b/drivers/clk/meson/s4-peripherals.c
index 9506df0..d986417 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/meson/s4-peripherals.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/meson/s4-peripherals.c
@@ -407,6 +407,7 @@
 			&s4_rtc_clk.hw
 		},
 		.num_parents = 2,
+		.flags = CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT,
 	},
 };
 
@@ -514,6 +515,7 @@
 			&s4_rtc_clk.hw
 		},
 		.num_parents = 2,
+		.flags = CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT,
 	},
 };
 
